# src/hook.aiw -- the places of build that the tests of interruption
# and of failed syncs need to reach, and the moments of search that the
# measurements tell apart, as the shipped executable has them:
# a stop point is nothing, and a sync is the sync. The executable of the
# tests is compiled with tests/lib/hook.aiw in the place of this file,
# and nothing of that one is in build/aildb.
#
# Every name of this file starts with "hook"; a program has no var of
# such a name.

const hookfsync 74

# the stop point hookn of build: 1 with the temporary file begun, 2 with
# it complete, synced and validated, before the rename, 3 after the
# rename, before the directory is synced; and of index, which publishes
# as build does: 4 before the publication, with the vectors kept, and 5
# after it, before the manifest is written
fn hookstop hookn
end

# flush the file hookfd to its device: 0, or the error of the kernel.
# hookn says which sync of build it is: 1 that of the temporary file, 2
# that of the directory.
fn hooksync hookfd hookn
	sys hookfsync hookfd as hookr
	ret hookr
end

# A moment of search that the measurements tell apart: 1 the program has
# started, 2 the snapshot is open and validated and the query is read, 3
# every record is scored, 4 the results are written. The shipped
# executable does nothing with it; the measurements, which are in the
# repository aildb-bench, compile the commands with a hook that notes
# the time.
fn hookmark hookn
end
